maestro-ticket: the maestro ticket store.

Usage: maestro-ticket <command> [flags]

Commands:
  create      --title T [--body B | --body-file F|-] [--type ship|scout] [--role R] [--priority 0-3]
              [--status backlog|todo|blocked (default todo)] [--owner NAME] [--deps T-1,T-2]
              [--areas path,path] [--split-from T-1] [--goal G] [--tier senior|junior]
              [--parked R (required for backlog)] [--lint (refuse an engineer's ship ticket with
              no numbered criterion, no Not handled: list or no areas)]
  update      <id> [--add-deps T-1,..] [--remove-deps T-1,..] [--areas path,..] [--parked R] [--goal G]
              [--tier senior|junior]
              [--split-from T-1 (a cancelled ticket this one replaces)] [--holder H --token N]
  get         <id> [--full]   (default: the newest comment of each kind, every Answer:, and the
              newest Handoff: and all after it in full; the rest as first lines)
  list        [--status S,...] [--role R] [--holder H] [--claimed | --unclaimed | --ready] [--limit N]
              [--latest-prefix P] [--not-latest-prefix P] [--parked R,...] [--goal G] [--tier T]
              [--bodies]   (ordered by priority, then id; no bodies: get prints one, and
              --bodies with --json each, for a search)
  goals       [--goal G] [--all]   (tickets per goal by status; --all adds goals with none open)
  log-run     [--ticket ID]   (reads a claude -p --output-format json reply on stdin, prints it
              unchanged, and records the session's cost and tokens; a resume replaces its total)
  costs       [--by actor|ticket|goal|origin|tries] [--ticket ID] [--since DATE|DURATION]
              (logged spend per group: runs, dollars, share, median per run and per ticket)
  flow        [--since DATE|DURATION] [--goal G]   (where done ship tickets spent their time:
              queue, build, review, QA and blocked, as median, p90 and share; how many review
              and QA sent back; the slowest three)
  alerts      [--stall 20m]   (each look's first step: frees what dead runs hold, then lists runs
              that died with no result, leases that ran out, missed ETAs, revived leases and
              in_review tickets with no one on them past --stall)
  look        [--limit N] [--judge] [--report] [--stall 20m]   (the planner's look in one call: alerts,
              the board, the fixed writes, worker jobs started as their bots, a line per message
              left to send, judge rows for the rest;
              --judge starts one judge session on them with the standing rules; the limit is
              rules set limit's, and --limit is a one-off)
  rules       [show] | set limit|qa_slots <n> | text | add | drop <n>   (the planner's limit, QA
              runs at once and the standing rules, which code reads; text and add read stdin; set
              outside a run by the planner, the chief of staff, the QA lead (qa_slots) or a person)
  eta         [--goal G --by TIME [--tickets T-1,..] | --goal G --clear]   (set, drop or list the
              times the owner was told goals would be ready; alerts reports a missed one)
  claim       (--next | <id>) --holder <bot-id>/<session-id> [--status S,...] [--role R] [--ttl 30m]
              [--keepalive PID]
  heartbeat   <id> --holder H --token N [--ttl 30m]
  keepalive   <id> --holder H --token N --pid PID [--ttl 30m] [--interval D]
  launch      [--ticket T-1] [--limit 2h] [--rings 0s,5m,10m,40m] -- claude -p [flags]
              (starts the run in the background, prompt on stdin, and returns its id)
  job         <job> [<id>...] [--model M] [--effort E] [--limit D]   (a bot's job as a Claude Code
              run: the prompt, model, effort, limit and session id set for it; text jobs read the
              ask on stdin, with --ticket T for the ticket it is about. build <id>, review <id> [--approved SHA] [--drop IDS --drop-file F|-]
              [--full], qa <id>, live <id>, qa-ask, plan, rule <id>, finish <id>, judge <id>..., cos,
              design <id>; again <run-id> [--limit D] [--full] starts a run's job afresh, flags kept)
  resume      <run-id> [--opus] [--escalate] [--decide] [--died]   (the run's session again,
              answer on stdin; --opus moves it to Opus high; --died resumes a dead run once)
  pickup      (shows each run you launched that ended and you haven't acked; lists yours still running)
  ack         <run-id>...   (you acted on its result: pickup stops showing it, its rings stop)
  stop        <run-id>   (ends a live run as its time limit would and records it failed, stopped
              by you; its launcher or the planner)
  stop        --all [--off]   (halts every claim and start, on every machine on the store; --off lifts it)
  runs        [<run-id>] [--all] [--launcher B]   (and claude -p sessions started outside launch)
  notify      [<bot-id>] [--url-file F|-] [--key-file F|-] [--clear] [--test]   (the webhook launch rings)
  release     <id> --holder H --token N [--died]
  reap
  transition  <id> --to S [--from S] [--expect-version N] [--holder H --token N] [--role R] [--note T] [--release]
              [--actor-role R] [--parked R (required to enter backlog, except back from blocked)]
  comment     <id> (--body B | --body-file F|-) [--holder H --token N]
  verdict     <id> --holder H --token N --body-file F|- --idempotency-key K   (a review's or QA's
              note and its move in one call, by the note's first line: Review: GO, QA: pass and
              Rereview: post only; a Kickback: sends the ticket back to in_progress; an
              Escalation: blocks it; refuses a review Kickback: that lists anything but blockers)
  handoff     <id> --holder H --token N --body-file F|- --idempotency-key K   (an engineer's
              Handoff: note, the move to in_review and the release, in one call)
  events      [--since SEQ] [--limit N] [--ticket ID] [--type T]
  backup      [--dir D] [--keep N]   (default dir: backups/ next to the store)
  export      [--out PATH|-]
  render      [--out PATH]     (default: Backlog.md next to the store)
  doctor
  store       [--uri-file F|- | --clear]   (writes store.uri, which puts the board on MongoDB, once
              the URI connects, or removes it; prints the store, with only the URI's host)
  migrate     --to mongodb [--uri-file F|-] | --to sqlite [--abort [--force]]   (moves the board between stores and
              checks the copy row by row; README's Move between stores says what each needs)
  slot        [--name checks] [--max 4] [--wait D] -- <command> [args]
              (runs the command once one of --max slots is free, so the sessions on
              one ticket store run at most that many at once, with a TMPDIR of its
