stderr:
Usage of maestro-ticket job:
  -actor string
    	who is acting
  -approved string
    	review: the head sha the owner said yes to
  -drop string
    	review: the finding ids a ruling dropped; the reason comes from --drop-file
  -drop-file string
    	review: read why the findings dropped from this file, or - for stdin
  -effort string
    	override the effort (default high)
  -full
    	review: on the full model, whatever the route
  -idempotency-key string
    	idempotency key for writes
  -json
    	machine-readable output
  -limit duration
    	override the time limit (default 2h; a review's is sized to its diff)
  -model string
    	override the job's model (opus or sonnet as a rule)
  -slots int
    	qa, live, qa-ask: QA runs at once on this store (default 6); the rest wait in line
  -store string
    	ticket store path
  -ticket string
    	the ticket a text job (qa-ask, plan, cos) works on
$ maestro-ticket resume --help
exit 0
stderr:
Usage of maestro-ticket resume:
  -actor string
    	who is acting
  -decide
    	resume a planner session that stopped on a question: it decides, or sends calls up
  -died
    	the run died: resume it once with "Your run died. Go on from your last step."
  -escalate
    	resume a build that ended on a question with "You stopped on a question. Post it on the ticket as an Escalation:, as maestro-working-principles says for a block, move the ticket to blocked, release it, and stop."
  -go-on
    	resume a session a usage limit stopped, once the limit lifts
  -idempotency-key string
    	idempotency key for writes
  -json
    	machine-readable output
  -opus
    	resume on Opus at high effort, as for a junior build's stuck session
  -store string
    	ticket store path
